[Music]  Opel's latest creation is the Crossland  x a subcompact crossover part SUV part  minivan it aims to combine the best of  both worlds  in other words generous space inside  with a fresh cutting edge look and the  cross land act certainly succeeds in  that octo a car testing Manawa Schaffer  mentions that the strongest growth is in  the B segment or small cars their sales  figures have doubled in the last four  years so car makers are scrambling to  roll out new B segment models opals  contribution is the Crossland X it  resembles its somewhat bigger brother  the mocha X but tones down the  sportiness and aggressive looks in  favour of greater practicality and  everyday driving we test-drove the  largest available engine the 1.2 liter  turbo gasoline with 96 kilowatts it  heaves the cross Lenox from 0 to 100  km/h in 9.1 seconds with a top speed of  260 kilometers per hour  [Music]  and mano-a-mano well explains that when  a car maker introduces a new model in a  segment they wanted to stand out from  its competitors Opel achieves this with  driver assists such as pedestrian  detection which the cross Lenox is the  first in its segment to offer  the front reveals the connection between  the mocha and the Crossland  opals logo is mounted on the grille  flanked by chrome winglets the embedded  low mounted fog lights emphasize its SUV  credentials the visible underbody  protection should do away with any  worries about scratch paint depending on  the trim level the colors of the side  mirrors and roof contrast with the rest  of the body  [Music]  a gently sloping roof contour recalls a  minivan LED tail lights are only offered  with the highest trim level the  selection as its called  [Music]  folding down the rear seats expands the  trunk volume from 410 to 1250 five  liters the interior gives a neat  impression many of the switches are set  on the steering wheel the 8 inch touch  infotainment system adds at least 650  euros to the price regardless of the  trim level air conditioning is standard  but automatic climate control only comes  with a selection line  [Music]  Opel is rolling out the Crossland X with  a range of five engines starting with a  1.2 liter gasoline engine with 60  kilowatts the most powerful though still  quiet fuel efficient is a 1.2 liter  turbo gasoline engine with 96 kilowatts  that's father Manuel describes the  Crossland axis suspension is offering  both comfort and sportiness though a bit  more comfort than sportiness he forgives  it slight tendency to roll the body sits  a little higher than normal  saying it's no problem and the car takes  curves nimbly and swiftly  [Music]  the Crossland X replaces the Mokka X as  the entry-level model for opals X range  the biggest model the Grande land X is  on its way  it will round off the x range at the  time prices for the cross flat x start  at just under 17,000 euros in Germany  but the 1.2 turbo edition we tested will  set you back at least 21 thousand euros  [Music]

